 and Ethics, Personal Development, and small unit tactics at the platoon level. At the conclusion of this course, you will be capable of planning, coordinating, navigating, motivating, and leading a squad or platoon in the execution of a mission. You will be required to write peer evaluations and receive feedback on your abilities as a leader and how to improve those leader skills that will further develop you as a successful officer. You will receive systematic and specific feedback on your leader attributes, values, and core leader competencies from your instructor, other ROTC cadre, and MSL IV Cadets who will evaluate you using the Cadet Officer Evaluation System.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "OT", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 351701, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "MILS", "catalogNbr": "3311", "titleShort": "Leadership Laboratory III", "titleLong": "Leadership Laboratory III", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LAB", "ssrComponentLong": "Laboratory", "section": "401", "classNbr": 11339, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "08:00AM", "timeEnd": "10:00AM", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [], "pattern": "F", "facilityDescr": "Barton Hall 100-Gym Floor", "bldgDescr": "Barton Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "BTN100", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/20/2023", 